    <statement><p>Let <m>f(x) = 4 x + 2</m> and <m>g(x) = 2 x^2 + 2 x</m>.
Match the functions obtained by composition with the letters labeling their algebraically equivalent expressions.</p>
<p>You must get all of the answers correct to receive credit.</p>
<p><ol>
<li>
<p><m>f \circ f</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>g \circ g</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>g \circ f</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>f \circ g</m></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
<p><ol label="A.">
<li>
<p><m>32 x^2 + 40 x + 12</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>16 x + 10</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>8 x^4 + 16 x^3 + 12 x^2 + 4 x</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>8 x^2 + 8 x + 2</m></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
